{
 "_meta": {
  "title": "wiki-sourced augment ACQUIRABILITY (#359)",
  "question": "Can a player obtain this augment without a specific named drop? The DDO wiki classifies every augment by rarity, and that taxonomy is the answer: Common/Uncommon/Rare augments are bought from vendors, traded for Mysterious Remnants or Collectables, or drop as generic loot. Named augments come from one specific source.",
  "why_it_exists": "Owned-augment mode (#359) restricts the augment pool to what a player can actually use. Restricting it to ONLY what their Trove export lists would delete ~88% of the pool, most of it augments nobody farms - you buy them. So the pool becomes owned UNION acquirable, and this file is the acquirable half.",
  "source": "https://ddowiki.com/page/Category:Common_augments, Category:Uncommon_augments, Category:Rare_augments - enumerated via action=query&list=categorymembers, paged, same-origin per docs/wiki-evidence/harvest-method.md",
  "corroboration": "Augment Slot/Purchasable Augments, verbatim: 'Augments drop randomly in level-appropriate chests ... but some (if not all) augments can also be bought in-game for items found or earned in the normal course of questing.' and 'Mysterious Remnants can be traded in for augments of ML 1-20.'",
  "not_listed_means": "NOT acquirable-by-default. The complement is Category:Named augments (1051 members) - drop-specific augments a player must actually own. Absence from this file is a positive statement, not a gap.",
  "harvested": "2026-08-20",
  "count": 675,
  "categories": {
   "Common augments": 668,
   "Uncommon augments": 6,
   "Rare augments": 1
  }
 },
